prompts.text:
Create a complete Game Design Document board in Milanote for this game:

{{game}}

Platform / engine: {{platform}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Structure to follow — this is the `gdd` template; every note below only describes what to write, replace all of it with real content for this game:

{{template:gdd}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}

Create a character sheet board in Milanote for:

{{character}}

Game: {{game}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Structure to follow — this is the `character_sheet` template; replace every descriptive note with real, specific content (real moves with real names, real stats relative to the roster):

{{template:character_sheet}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}

Create a level design board in Milanote for:

{{level}}

Game: {{game}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Structure to follow — this is the `level_design` template; replace every descriptive note with the real design (named zones, concrete encounters, actual dimensions where you can):

{{template:level_design}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}

Brainstorm this topic and capture the result as a Milanote board:

{{topic}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Aim for 8–12 distinct ideas (one note each, with a one-line "why it might work"), 3–5 open questions, the real constraints, two wild cards (one too ambitious, one embarrassingly simple) and concrete next steps as a to-do list. Structure (the `brainstorm` template — replace the descriptive text):

{{template:brainstorm}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}

Build a mood board in Milanote for:

{{theme}}

References from the user: {{references}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Give the direction in concrete terms (three adjectives, a hex palette, named materials and shapes) and put every reference in its own bare ### section as a URL with a short caption so Milanote shows a preview card. Structure (the `moodboard` template — replace the descriptive text):

{{template:moodboard}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}

Plan this project as a Milanote board:

{{project}}

Deadline: {{deadline}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Milestones must be to-do lists with concrete, checkable tasks; the backlog holds everything else; "This week" gets the 3–6 tasks to start now. Structure (the `project_plan` template — replace the descriptive text):

{{template:project_plan}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}

Organise these raw notes from "{{meeting}}" into a Milanote board:

{{notes}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Keep the original wording where it matters, do not invent decisions or actions that are not in the notes, and put every action item in the to-do list with its owner and due date when the notes give them. Structure (the `meeting_notes` template — replace the descriptive text):

{{template:meeting_notes}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}

Create a weekly plan board in Milanote.

Week: {{week}}
Focus and known commitments: {{focus}}

{{snippet:workflow}}

Spread the work realistically over the weekdays (3–5 tasks a day, hardest first), keep the top-3 outcomes tied to the focus, and leave Friday room for review. Structure (the `weekly_plan` template — replace the descriptive text):

{{template:weekly_plan}}

{{snippet:outline_format}}
